        "thread_id": "TH3",
        "thread_goal": "Plan and monitor drainage upgrades and pipe bedding works",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M39",
            "speaker_id": 168084,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Team, we're starting on the drainage upgrades for T5. The existing channel in the first section is more damaged than we thought. The standard detail in A5 might not work here. Any thoughts?",
            "mentions": [
              70034,
              6789
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T5",
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M40",
            "speaker_id": 6789,
            "reply_to": "M39",
            "text": "Can you post a photo? I can come take a look. We need to get the pipe bedding right or we'll be back here in a year.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M41",
            "speaker_id": 168084,
            "reply_to": "M40",
            "text": "Photo attached. The channel wall has collapsed in a few places.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M42",
            "speaker_id": 70034,
            "reply_to": "M41",
            "text": "I see. We can't use the standard detail from A5 there. We'll need to over-excavate and form a new channel edge with compacted base before laying the pipe. It's more work but it's the right way to do it.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M43",
            "speaker_id": 384719,
            "reply_to": "M42",
            "text": "Will that need different pipes?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M44",
            "speaker_id": 70034,
            "reply_to": "M43",
            "text": "No, same pipes, just a more robust foundation for them. Let's make a decision on this. Decision: Where existing drainage channels are damaged, we will use a modified detail: over-excavate the damaged section and form a new edge with compacted base material before pipe installation.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_check_mark",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M45",
            "speaker_id": 6789,
            "reply_to": "M44",
            "text": "Agreed. That's the proper fix. Now, for quality control, we need to be strict. How about we set clear inspection points for T10?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T10"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M46",
            "speaker_id": 70034,
            "reply_to": "M45",
            "text": "Good idea. Let's use the Quality Checklist A6. Decision: We will have two mandatory inspection points for all drainage works before backfilling: 1) after excavation to check the trench base, and 2) after pipe laying to check slope and bedding. Both must be signed off on A6.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D6"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "clipboard",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M47",
            "speaker_id": 168084,
            "reply_to": "M46",
            "text": "Perfect, that's clear. We'll follow that process. Thanks.",
            "mentions": [],
